* Objects for the mq-metric-samples TLS end-to-end test.
* Runs after the developer defaults (10-dev.mqsc) and the TLS setup (15/20-*.mqsc).

* A queue to put test messages on
DEFINE QLOCAL('MON.TEST.QUEUE') MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE

* Dedicated SVRCONN for the monitor. The client MUST present a certificate.
* MCAUSER is set to a blocked id so that the only way in is through the
* CHLAUTH mapping below.
DEFINE CHANNEL('MON.SVRCONN') CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) TRPTYPE(TCP) +
       SSLCIPH(ANY_TLS12_OR_HIGHER) SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) MCAUSER('nobody') REPLACE

* Map the monitor's certificate DN to the mqmon identity. SSLPEERMAP rules
* take precedence over the developer config's ADDRESSMAP back-stop rule.
SET CHLAUTH('MON.SVRCONN') TYPE(SSLPEERMAP) SSLPEER('CN=mqmon,O=e2e') +
    USERSRC(MAP) MCAUSER('mqmon') CHCKCLNT(ASQMGR) +
    DESCR('Monitor client certificate -> mqmon') ACTION(REPLACE)

* Anything else arriving on this channel is refused.
SET CHLAUTH('MON.SVRCONN') TYPE(ADDRESSMAP) ADDRESS('*') USERSRC(NOACCESS) +
    DESCR('Block unmapped connections on MON.SVRCONN') ACTION(REPLACE)

* Minimum authorities for the collector (read-only monitoring).
* The container image sets MQS_PERMIT_UNKNOWN_ID so mqmon needs no OS account.
SET AUTHREC PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(QMGR) AUTHADD(CONNECT,INQ,DSP)
* PCF commands are sent to the command queue
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.COMMAND.QUEUE') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) AUTHADD(PUT)
* Replies and publications arrive on dynamic queues built from the model queue
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.DEFAULT.MODEL.QUEUE') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) AUTHADD(GET,INQ,DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('AMQ.**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) AUTHADD(GET,INQ,DSP)
* Resource metrics are published under $SYS/MQ (SYSTEM.ADMIN.TOPIC)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.TOPIC') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(TOPIC) AUTHADD(SUB)
* DISPLAY xxSTATUS needs DSP on the objects being displayed
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(QUEUE)   AUTHADD(DSP,INQ)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(CHANNEL) AUTHADD(DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(TOPIC)   AUTHADD(DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(CLNTCONN) AUTHADD(DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(LISTENER) AUTHADD(DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') PRINCIPAL('mqmon') OBJTYPE(SERVICE)  AUTHADD(DSP)

* Log authority failures as events too, handy when tightening the list above
ALTER QMGR AUTHOREV(ENABLED)
REFRESH SECURITY(*)
